Zeo patch 0004 — nudge a model that announces a tool call instead of making it.

Target: Open WebUI v0.11.4 (ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:v0.11.4).
Applied by ai/openwebui/Dockerfile.openwebui with `patch -p1` from /app.

Upstream: with native function calling the backend runs the tool loop
(utils/middleware.py, streaming_chat_response_handler): tool calls are run
and the model asked again, and the first reply WITHOUT tool calls ends the
turn. Local models (muse-glimmer via LiteLLM) regularly end a turn right
after a tool result by announcing the next step instead of taking it —
"Permission denied on `/app/test.js` via exec. I'll use `write_files` to
create the test harness correctly, then run it." — and nothing happens until
the user types "go on".

This patch checks that final reply before the loop ends. When ALL hold:
native function calling with tools offered, at least one tool round ran this
turn and the reply came straight after a tool result, the reply (LiteLLM
`auto` footer stripped, code removed, reasoning excluded) ends in first-person
forward-looking intent ("let me", "I'll", "I'm going to", "give me a
moment", ...) and hands nothing back to the user (no question, no offer
such as "tell me and I'll check" or "if you're in X, ..."), and fewer than
AUTO_CONTINUE_MAX_NUDGES nudges were sent this turn — it sends the
conversation plus a hidden user message ("You said you would take an action
but your reply contained no tool call ...") through the same continuation
path a tool round uses. The continuation, and any tool calls it makes (which
then run through the normal loop), are appended to the same assistant
message. The nudge exists only in that one request: it is never shown in the
chat and never saved. One INFO line per nudge: `auto-continue: chat <id>
nudge k/N: ...`.

AUTO_CONTINUE_MAX_NUDGES (compose: ${OPENWEBUI_AUTO_CONTINUE_MAX_NUDGES:-2})
caps nudges per assistant turn; 0 turns the feature off. Legacy function
calling, task-model calls and the non-streaming handler (which has no tool
loop) are untouched; the Responses-API stateful mode (previous_response_id)
is skipped.

Files: backend/open_webui/utils/middleware.py,
       backend/open_webui/utils/zeo_auto_continue.py (new).
See ai/openwebui/OPENWEBUI.md § Auto-continue announced tool calls and
§ Custom image. Tests: unit-tests/openwebui/ (load the new module straight
out of this file).

